<title>GERMANY: German grain area in 1997 up 5 pct -ZMP data.</title>
<headline>German grain area in 1997 up 5 pct -ZMP data.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Data from Germany's farm price office ZMP showed the 1997 grain area was up from 1996 by five percent at 7.04 million hectares.</p>
<p>ZMP developed the figures on the basis of plantings information received by federal and state statistics offices and regional agricultural chambers.</p>
<p>The Bonn farm ministry said its official area figures would not be presented before next month.</p>
<p>The figures showed the combined spring, winter and durum wheat area had increased by 2.4 percent to 2.66 million, while the combined winter and spring barley area rose 7.3 percent to 2.37 million ha.</p>
<p>Rye was up by 2.5 percent at 831,844 ha while triticale increased by 30.3 percent to 478,170 and maize dropped by 6.4 percent to 352,412 ha.</p>
<p>ZMP gave the following details (in ha) --</p>
<p>					 1996	     1997</p>
<p>    winter wheat		 2,543,521	 2,587,452</p>
<p>    spring wheat		    42,884	    62,374</p>
<p>    durum				8,013	     7,616</p>
<p>    rye				809,052	   831,844</p>
<p>    winter barley		1,413,062	 1,510,570</p>
<p>    spring barley		  795,345	   843,804</p>
<p>    oats			     301,888	   304,674</p>
<p>    triticale			364,224	   478,170</p>
<p>    maize for silage	     277,254	   275,173</p>
<p>    corn/cob maize		  94,862	    77,239</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
